          "properties": {
            "tags": [
              "DATADOG_CONFIDENCE:HIGH",
              "DATADOG_CONFIDENCE_REASON:The logic flaw resides in the 'verifyAccount' method (referenced in line 58). As described, the method validates account verification based on the presence and content of security questions. If the implementation fails to enforce required keys and only conditionally validates keys present in the map, a user can bypass verification by submitting arbitrary keys that evade the validation logic. This is an authentication bypass vulnerability via a logic error in the authorization check. Source: User-controlled HttpServletRequest. Sink: The verifyAccount method call at line 58. Conclusion: Confirmed."
            ]
          },
          "ruleId": "datadog/java-xss",
          "ruleIndex": 7,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "The logic flaw resides in the 'verifyAccount' method (referenced in line 58). As described, the method validates account verification based on the presence and content of security questions. If the implementation fails to enforce required keys and only conditionally validates keys present in the map, a user can bypass verification by submitting arbitrary keys that evade the validation logic. This is an authentication bypass vulnerability via a logic error in the authorization check. Source: User-controlled HttpServletRequest. Sink: The verifyAccount method call at line 58. Conclusion: Confirmed."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
